<title>USA: Wells Fargo puts job cut tally at 13,800.</title>
<headline>Wells Fargo puts job cut tally at 13,800.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wells Fargo and Co on Friday said it expects to have about 32,000 full-time employees by the fourth quarter of 1997, versus 45,800 in April 1996, when it merged with First Interstate Bancorp.</p>
<p>The company's expected headcount for late 1997 reflects the elimination of 13,800 jobs since the merger was completed.</p>
<p>Wells Fargo's forecast was published in its 10Q filed with the Securities Exchange Commission this week. A Wells Fargo spokeswoman said the company released the same forecast in last quarter's 10Q. As of June 30, the company's active full-time equivalent staff was 33,216.</p>
</text>
